    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Cloudzy VPS Review 2026: EPYC + DDR5 + 40 Gbps from $2.48/mo</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8">Published 2026-07-31 · Independent Dubai operator since 2008 · Verified pricing + datacenter data from cloudzy.com</p>

    <div class="bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
        <span class="text-2xl font-bold">4.4/5</span>
        <span class="text-gray-500">Developer Rating</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
        Cloudzy (formerly RouterHosting) is an independent self-funded cloud provider headquartered in Dubai, UAE, operating continuously since 2008 — 18 years without acquisition or VC funding. The pitch is unusual at the $2.48/mo entry tier: AMD EPYC CPUs, DDR5 memory, pure NVMe storage, and 40 Gbps networking on every single plan, with 13 datacenters spanning North America, Europe, and Asia-Pacific. The provider serves 122,000+ developers and businesses, holds a 4.6/5 Trustpilot rating, accepts Monero (XMR) directly alongside Bitcoin and USDT, and publishes a 99.95% uptime SLA with a 14-day unconditional money-back guarantee. The differentiator vs the budget tier (<a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd</a>, BuyVM) is not raw $/GB — Cloudzy loses on that axis — but the bundle of DDR5 + 40 Gbps + multi-DC + 18-year self-funded track record + UAE jurisdiction + XMR acceptance, which most budget providers do not assemble in one place.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-3 text-sm">Entry: $2.48/mo (promo) · 1GB: $3.48/mo · 4GB: $14.48/mo · 64GB: $199.98/mo · 50% promo in effect</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4">Introduction and Quick Specs</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Cloudzy is an independent self-funded cloud provider founded in 2008 and headquartered in Dubai, UAE. The legal entity is Cloudzy AI Information Technology L.L.C. (a UAE Free Zone limited liability company). The provider has served 122,000+ developers and businesses across 18 years of continuous operation, never raising a dollar of VC funding and never being acquired. The 2024 rebrand from RouterHosting to Cloudzy consolidated the legacy identity into a single global brand; the underlying infrastructure, operator, and customer base carried over unchanged. The current infrastructure is uniformly modern: AMD EPYC CPUs (Regular line) or AMD Ryzen 4.2 GHz+ (High-Frequency line), DDR5 memory, pure NVMe storage (no SATA or hybrid tiers anywhere in the matrix), and 40 Gbps per-node uplinks on every tier from the $2.48/mo entry up.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      This review covers the four dimensions most buyers care about: pricing transparency (including the 50% promotional pricing caveat), infrastructure modernity (DDR5 + EPYC + 40 Gbps story), datacenter footprint (13 active nodes + Tokyo coming soon), and the editorial positioning vs RackNerd (cheapest) and Vultr (hyperscaler-grade managed). It also flags three things Cloudzy is <em>not</em> (managed services, cheapest possible $/GB, hyperscaler-grade 99.99%+ SLA) and names three close substitutes on this site for buyers whose requirements don't match.
    </p>

